  "views": {
    "hero": "three_quarter",
    "reads": {
      "front": "From behind the bard: the glyph circle lies flat around them, golden rings roll outward across the ground one per beat, small ripples bloom off the instrument at hand height and motes rise all around.",
      "side": "The rings read as thin bright lines sliding along the ground; the hand ripples and the rising motes give it height, and a warm glow wraps the bard.",
      "top": "The best read of the music: three concentric rings spread evenly from the bard over a turning glyph circle, and motes speckle the whole area.",
      "three_quarter": "Hero view. The rings are ellipses rolling out across the ground in rhythm, the glyph circle turns under them and motes drift up through the field."
    }
