  "variation": {
    "seeded": true,
    "notes": "The glyph textures, the mote positions and the instrument sparkle change per cast. The downbeat rhythm (a ring every 500 ms) stays fixed so it can sync to music."
  },
  "director_notes": "From Lisa's spells01 image, Bard - Anthem: golden concentric sound rings and lyre glyphs that inspire allies. Original take, no game's art. Rings are timed as downbeats 500 ms apart so an engine can retime them to a song's tempo. Each downbeat stacks a crisp ring, a soft echo band behind it and a small billboard ripple at the instrument so the music reads in every view. A rune circle stands in for the lyre glyphs (the engine should swap in real lyre and stave glyphs). Motes rise over the whole footprint for the buff. Sound: a shimmer strum, a high hum and a chime on each downbeat; replace with the real song in an engine."
}
